Vita (--vita-skip-hidden-draw=off|on, platform/vita/runtime/visual_skips.hpp): a visual-only
speed-up (the picture may change, the game may not). With fixed game ticks (0015) a loop may run
two ticks before it paints, and the paint shows only the last one: each draw phase resets the draw
lists. On, in the draw phase of a tick that another tick follows (and no menu capture stops the
loop after it), fopAc_Draw does not call an actor's draw method; the event check, the culling test,
the "not drawn" condition and the NODRAW status still update, as execute reads them. Types whose
draw does game work stay on the full path (twv_draw_keep). The check is the game-state digest
(--vita-state-digest): the same game, tick for tick, with the skip on and off.
game_clock: the running tick's index in its loop, and whether another tick follows it.

